  "Description":      "Response and Scene Rendering: renders the machine's response - a Text - as a Speaking Avatar of the input Avatar Model, ready to play; whoever requested it places it in a scene and renders it. Personal Status De-multiplexing splits a supplied Personal Status into the Speech, Face and Body Personal Statuses that make the avatar expressive - neutral without one; Text-To-Speech makes the Machine Speech; Speaking Avatar Formation forms the Speaking Avatar. This Implementation takes no Speech Model and no Input Speech (both optional in the AIM).",

